# =============================================================================
# IoTmx API — Authentication
#
# The login handshake uses AES-256-GCM + HKDF-SHA256.  Raw .http tools
# cannot compute HKDF, so use the e2e.py helper for login and all subsequent
# protected calls.
#
# Quick start:
#   uv run python http/e2e.py login master_admin@test.com MasterPassword123!
#
# After login the session is saved to .e2e_session.json.
# Copy the printed SESSION_ID into http-client.env.json to use the GET
# requests below directly from VS Code REST Client.
# =============================================================================

@base_url = http://localhost:8000
@session_id = {{$dotenv SESSION_ID}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Step 1 — Challenge (public, plaintext)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Get challenge for master admin
GET {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/challenge?email=master_admin@test.com


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Step 2 — Login (public endpoint, but body/response are E2E-encrypted)
#
# The body below shows the WIRE FORMAT (not the plaintext you type).
# e2e.py generates it automatically — you never construct this by hand.
#
# Wire request body:
#   username   — the email address
#   payload    — AES-256-GCM({"random2": <64-hex-char>}, temp_key), base64
#   random     — 32-hex-char random used to derive temp_key (HKDF)
#   iv         — 12-byte GCM nonce, base64
#
# Wire response (encrypted with temp_key):
#   {"session-id": "...", "random3": "..."}
#
# USE:
#   uv run python http/e2e.py login <email> <password> [--url URL]
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Login — WIRE FORMAT reference (do not send manually; use e2e.py)
# POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# {
#   "username": "master_admin@test.com",
#   "payload":  "<base64-AES-256-GCM ciphertext>",
#   "random":   "<32-hex>",
#   "iv":       "<base64-12-byte nonce>"
# }


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Session management (protected — need X-Session-ID from login)
# All responses are AES-256-GCM encrypted; use e2e.py to auto-decrypt.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Renew session (extend TTL)
# e2e.py: uv run python http/e2e.py post /api/v1/auth/renew '{}'
POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/renew
Content-Type: application/json
X-Session-ID: {{session_id}}

{}

###

### Logout (terminates session in Valkey)
# e2e.py: uv run python http/e2e.py logout
POST {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json
X-Session-ID: {{session_id}}

{}

###

### Change password
# e2e.py: uv run python http/e2e.py patch /api/v1/auth/change-password \
#   '{"old_password":"OldPass123!","new_password":"NewPass456@"}'
#
# Plaintext body:
PATCH {{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Session-ID: {{session_id}}

{
  "payload": "<AES-256-GCM encrypted — use e2e.py>",
  "iv": "<base64 nonce>"
}
